@startuml resolve
' SPEC: _spec/packages/starchess-core/resolve.puml
' purpose: Rank-major resolve — turn-open king-checks (before intent) → End: B → C → F.
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/resolve/resolve-turn.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/resolve/submit-turn.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/__tests__/rook/**
' see also: _spec/packages/starchess-core/gas-phase-vacancy.puml
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

title StarChess · Resolve — 3 phases: attack → move → fog approach

start

:Take planning snap — turn N is open;

:**Turn-open legal king-checks** — ""beginScTurn"" — fog-visible, implicit,\nwhite then black — ""applyPendingCCShots"".\nResolved **before** players choose intent. A unit that\nbreaks contact later this turn already paid a **parting shot**;

if (the two kings are adjacent?) then (yes)
  :**King duel** — a king is a legal checker of the enemy king.\nThe collector loops **both** king colours independently, so\ncontact is always **mutual**. Damage is **per checker**: every\nunit checking a king costs it 1 HP, so N checkers = N HP.\nKings leap — ""leapsPiece"" — never the blocker / collision\nbranch: adjacency always chips, nothing is captured, the\nplacement is untouched;
else (no)
  :Only checkers with clear geometry to the king chip;
endif

if (either king at 0 HP after turn-open checks?) then (yes)
  :Phase O — no intent / B / C / F;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Players queue intent (specials + classical);

:End / timeout — ""endScTurn"" — live passes\n""skipTurnStartChecks"" when checks already applied;

:Apply rank **B** specials — white then black\n— spawn / mine / warp / siege;\n**Presentation:** gas absorb VFX — canister drops\nfrom the top of the actor square — left / mid / right —\ninto the unit; green special-used aura eases in;

note right
  **Arrivals × mine** (""applyArrivalMine"") — mines are **never occupancy**, so a
  mined tile is always a legal landing (""tacticalJumpTargets"" only drops occupied
  squares). None of these **attack** the tile, so a **hostile** mine detonates on
  arrival — mine and arriving unit both die; an **allied** mine stays armed and
  inert underfoot:
  * **Tactical Jump** — the jump teleports; BattleShip and mine both die
    (cues ""qj"" hull → ""qjm"" boom → ""qjd"" wreck, all pre-""afterB"");
  * **gas step** (""stimStep"", B **and** F) — the marine hops, then the mine
    takes it; a last-rank step dies **without promoting**;
  * **deploy** (""spawn"") — the drop plays, then the fresh unit dies with the
    mine; a crushed ally or enemy occupant still reports as ""victim"" (one tile, two deaths).
  Events carry ""mineColor"" + the dead hull as ""victim"" (a mined ""spawn"" names
  its unit in ""unit""); cues ""armm"" boom → ""armd"" wreck.
  The Adjutant never queues a step / drop onto a mine it can see.
end note

:Rank **C** — classical for both sides against\nthe same start board — ""resolveTurn"";

note right
  A B relocate that departs
  relinquishes its origin for all
  subsequent landings this turn.
  Ordered resolve retires the mover
  before recording any arrival.
end note

:Phase 1 **attack** — direct attacks on targets visible\nfrom the start board — attack → death → occupy;

note right
  **A mine is a target, not a wall.** The tile is attacked when the mover
  *attacks where it lands* (""attacksOwnDest"") — every unit but a **marine
  forward step** (marines only attack front diagonals) — the mine is **lit for
  that side**, and the tile is **reachable** (no blocker on the ray). Otherwise
  the intent stays a quiet step and the mine takes the mover in phase 2:
  * marine forward step onto a mine → **both die**, promotion cancelled;
  * mine still **fogged** at contact → walk-over death (never a chosen target);
  * mine **crossed mid-slide** → chase wake → both die at the landing tile.
    Marines walk, so a **front double step** wakes a mine on its intermediate
    exactly like a slide (""pathContactSquares"" — only leaping Hoverbikes and
    kings skip the ray). An **Extra Step** extends that walk by one hop, so the
    wake chases onto the marine's real destination whichever way the queue was
    ordered (""mine-contact.puml"" · one walk per marine);
  * a **king** never trades: its contact is an attack in every mode, so it
    clears the tile and moves in (""mine-contact.puml"");
  * **allied** mines are inert underfoot (no friendly fire).
end note

note right
  **A marine never attacks forward.** Marines only ever fire on their front
  **diagonals**, so a straight advance is a walk, not a shot: a unit anywhere
  on the forward path **blocks** it — no attack cue, no move collision, no fog
  discovery, whatever the fog says. The marine truncates onto the last empty
  square before the blocker, exactly like an ally-blocked slide:
  * ""d2→d3"" with **d3** held → the marine stays on **d2**;
  * ""d2→d4"" with **d4** held — an enemy gassed in first — → it stops on **d3**;
  * ""d2→d4"" with **d3** held → it stays on **d2**: a marine walks, never leaps;
  * an enemy **king** ahead blocks like any unit — no HP chip, no discovery;
  * front **diagonals** are untouched — enemy capture and mine clearing stand;
  * **head-on race** — two marines onto the same *empty* square still both die
    in phase 2. Neither attacked; they collided.
end note

if (attack hits a piece?) then (yes)
  :Death — victim removed;
  if (attacker survives?) then (yes)
    :**Occupy** victim's square;
  else (no)
    :Attacker dies first — square stays empty, no occupy;
  endif
elseif (attack hits a visible hostile **mine**?) then (yes)
  :""mineBlast"" in ""attacks"" — the **mine** dies (no victim);\nattacker **occupies** the tile — a sieged tank clears it\nwithout relocating (""firesInPlace"");
else (no)
  if (sieged rook shells empty cross?\nempty ""to"" on file/rank, clear ray, visible) then (yes)
    :""shelling"" in ""attacks"" — victimless HE at ""to"";\nno death, no occupy, tank holds (""firesInPlace"");\nclear ray only — mid-ray enemy captured upstream,\nally/king contact holds fire, fogged stays quiet;
  else (no)
    :No direct hit — quiet intent defers to phase 2;
  endif
endif

:Phase 2 **move** — survivors relocate; collisions\nresolved against the post-attack board; a target\n**still fogged at contact** → move collision\n— capture/occupy, no attack cue (never a\n**marine front step** — that blocks + truncates);\n**same-square race** (two movers land on one tile)\n→ **both die**, square empty, no attack cue;

:Phase 3 **fog approach** — path-reveal shots slide\n""pathRevealFrom"" → discovery square → attack;\n**King HP mid-resolve** only here: fog intent finds a\nhidden king on the path — ""pathReveal"" ccShot.\nVisible kings already paid at turn open — no second chip.\n**fizzle unless** the attacker still occupies\n""pathRevealFrom"" — died in phases 1–2 / square\nre-occupied by a phase-2 mover / sieged — rooks\nnever relocate — and ""to"" holds the exact\nin-the-way victim;

note right
  **Approach × mine.** A fog approach **walks** its ray — origin → discovery →
  landing tile (""to"" for a capture, ""stopAt"" for a ccShot) — so a **hostile**
  mine anywhere on that walk takes the mover, and the approach never *clears*
  one (it chose a unit, not the tile). The shot already fired, so the capture /
  HP chip **stands** and the mover dies on its landing tile:
  * mine **mid-walk** → chase wake → ""chaseFrom"" (missile then boom);
  * mine on the **landing tile** → plain walk-over boom;
  * **allied** mines stay inert. A king never reaches here at all — kings
    leap, so they never slide into fog.
  Blasts land in ""pathRevealMineTriggers"" (cues ""prmm"" missile → ""prm"" boom →
  ""prv"" wreck, replayed off the ""afterMove"" mine snapshot).
end note

:Apply rank **F** specials — white then black\n— post-move siege / late drops;\n**Presentation:** same gas absorb drop + aura as B;

if (either king at 0 HP after all ranks?) then (yes)
  :Next snap phase **O** — terminal and **absorbing**;
  :""endScTurn"" throws on a non-P snapshot;
  :""scOutcome"" from ccLives — 0/0 draw, else win;
else (no)
  :Next snap phase **P** — play continues;
endif

note right
  **Promotion (after move/mine):** relocate lands a **pawn**; survivors with
  a queued promotion then **walk off** the board edge (1× ""MOVE_SQUARE_MS"")
  and the chosen unit **deploys**. A promoting pawn that **walks onto** a
  hostile mine (forward step — pawns only attack front diagonals) dies with
  the mine — **no** walk-off / deploy. Units that attack the mine square
  clear it in the attack phase then occupy — including a marine that
  **promotes by taking a last-rank mine on its front diagonal**.
  Completed-history wire ""C=from intentTo>resolvedTo"" remains **deferred**.
end note

stop

note right
  **Intent ""C="" vs progressive path resolve:** ""pathRevealSteps"" /
  ""pathRevealFrom"" in ""resolveTurn"" capture the fog approach — now a
  **phase-3** event: the attacker slides from ""pathRevealFrom"" to the
  discovery square, then attacks, applied **after** moves. An approach
  **fizzles** when the attacker no longer occupies ""pathRevealFrom""
  (died in phases 1–2, or its square was re-occupied by a phase-2 mover
  — ""destinationsWritten""), when the origin is sieged (""siegedTanks""
  — rooks never relocate), or when ""to"" no longer holds the exact
  in-the-way victim (""a.victim"" color+type): empty, a converging
  same-side ally, or a different enemy not in the way — never captured.
  Sieged rooks also **fizzle fogged contact** — they never relocate, so
  a fogged adjacent (or never-revealed) target and a fogged mine square
  are not attacked; visible targets still die to the turret.
  ""applyPathRevealAttack(snap, a)"" is the shared source of truth for the
  board-state fizzles (attacker still on ""pathRevealFrom"", exact victim on
  ""to""); the engine loop pre-filters the siege (""siegedTanks"") and
  origin-re-occupation (""destinationsWritten"") gates before the attack is
  listed, and the UI replay (""playTimeline"" / MatchStore ""TIMELINE_*"")
  replays only that fired list, so
  ""pathRevealAttacks"" holds **only attacks that fired**.
  ""resolveTurn"" returns ""attacks"" (phase 1),
  ""moves"" / ""mineTriggers"" / ""moveCollisions"" (phase 2),
  ""pathRevealAttacks"" + ""pathRevealMineTriggers"" (phase 3), and the
  snapshots ""afterMove"" (post-phase-2) and ""afterAll"" (post-phase-3).
  ""applyPathRevealAttack"" leaves mines armed — the walk-contact check that
  spends them lives in the phase-3 loop next to it.
  **King shots:** ""collectLegalCCChecks"" + ""applyPendingCCShots""
  via ""beginScTurn"" at turn open (before intent). The **only** mid-resolve
  king HP is fog path-discovery (""applyPathRevealCCShot""): intent into
  fog finds a hidden king on the ray. Live ""endScTurn"" skips re-application
  of turn-open checks (""skipTurnStartChecks""); atomic replay may still run
  checks inside ""endScTurn"". No king-aimed ""C="".
  ====
  **King duel — two adjacent kings fight face-to-face.**
  ""collectLegalCCChecks"" does **not** exclude king-type attackers, so a
  king is a legal implicit checker of the enemy king. The collector loops
  both king colours independently, so contact is always **mutual**.
  Damage is **per checking unit**, not capped per turn: every unit that
  checks a king takes 1 HP off it, so N checkers cost N HP in one pass.
  A lone duel is therefore 1 HP each way at turn start.
  * **Kings leap** (""leapsPiece"" includes 'k'), so a duel never takes the
    blocker / collision branch: adjacency always chips, nothing is
    captured, the placement is returned untouched.
  * **Firing is never gated on the shooter's own HP** — only on board
    occupancy and target identity. A king reduced to 0 in the **same** pass
    still returns fire. Deliberate and load-bearing: it is what makes equal
    HP end 0/0 a **draw** instead of a win for whoever is ordered first
    (white sorts first). ""resolveTurn"" carries a comment warning against
    //fixing// it.
  * **Equal HP** drains 3/3 → 2/2 → 1/1 → 0/0 and flips phase to ""O""
    (a draw). **Unequal HP**: the lower king dies first.
  * **Deploy race** — a king deploys onto its own adjacent ring, so a unit
    spawned next to the enemy king stacks a **second** checker. Per-checker
    damage then chips **2 HP/turn** while taking 1. The doubling is an
    intended feature of the rule, and follows from the per-checker rule
    rather than being a special case.
  * **Parting shot** — pendings are computed before the move phase, so a
    king that breaks contact still loses 1 HP that turn.
  * **Immediate exit** — the moment a king is left at 0 HP the turn **bails
    out**: from the check phase nothing else resolves at all (no B, C or F),
    and from the classical pass no F special resolves behind the dead king
    (""endScTurn"" returns a terminal result at both seams). The classical
    pass is simultaneous, so it completes as one unit before the far-side
    bail out. Both shots of a duel are already applied, so mutual death
    still reads 0/0 = draw.
  * **Fog-discovered check** — the mid-path king chip is deliberately **not**
    fog-gated, unlike the turn-start check. A slider with no vision of the
    enemy king still chips it by walking its ray into it: that is a
    //discovered check//, which is a plain check once the fog is lifted, so
    the damage stands. The mover stops **before** the king (never occupies
    it), and such a killing blow bails the turn out like any other.
  Phase ""O"" is **absorbing** (""endScTurn"" throws on a non-""P"" snapshot),
  and ""parseScFen"" rejects a 0-HP side outside phase ""O"" so a dead king
  can never sit in a playable snapshot.
  ""scOutcome(snap)"" (""outcome.ts"") returns ""{winner:'w'}"" /
  ""{winner:'b'}"" for a win, ""{winner:null,draw:true}"" for a draw, or
  ""null"" while play continues — derived purely from
  ""ccLives"". HP is the single source of truth, so there is no
  persisted winner field and **no SCFEN grammar change**
  (wire grammar unchanged; ""O"" was already a valid phase code).
  Covered by core unit tests under ""packages/starchess-core""
  (historical path: ""packages/starchess-core/src/__tests__/"" (king duel / beginScTurn)).
end note
@enduml
